into the DNS records of your domain name. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:06.680 --> 01:43:15.400
then people can send — like, I've got Drew.com.&nbsp;
I can use that as my Bitcoin wallet. And I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:15.400 --> 01:43:21.920
that — so first feature of why I believe there's&nbsp;
this huge growth curve coming for domain names.&nbsp;

01:43:21.920 --> 01:43:30.400
First is identity KYC. Okay? Second is finance&nbsp;
and wallets, specifically wallets, because again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:30.400 --> 01:43:33.920
it's the same problem. It's like, "Yes,&nbsp;
you can use some of these Web3 domains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:33.920 --> 01:43:39.920
these .eth," and I was one of the first investors&nbsp;
into unstoppable domains. I was literally probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

