Andrew Rosener: Totally. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:57.520 --> 01:46:01.224
even if they're not bad actors, there's just&nbsp;
going to be a tremendous amount of confusion.&nbsp;

01:46:01.224 --> 01:46:02.720
Tim Ferriss: Confusion, confusion. Yeah.
Andrew Rosener: Because you say, "Hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:02.720 --> 01:46:06.880
send me an ETH to the tim.wallet," but&nbsp;
depending on which wallet I'm using,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:06.880 --> 01:46:12.960
which wallet software I'm using, I don't know if&nbsp;
that's going to the Ethereum blockchain. Is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:12.960 --> 01:46:18.840
going to the Handshake blockchain? Is that going&nbsp;
to the Unstoppable? Which blockchain is that on?&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:18.840 --> 01:46:25.760
And so I could send it to Tim.wallet and it could&nbsp;
go to a different Tim.wallet, and I have, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:25.760 --> 01:46:30.880
nothing I can do about that unless I've got some&nbsp;
degree of tech-savvy and I can pull down a menu&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:30.880 --> 01:46:35.080
